# Copy this file to `.env` if you need the Firebase backend.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# You do NOT need any of this to browse and search the archive. The photo index is
# generated from the images in this repository and ships with the site, so
# `npm run start` shows all 2948 photographs on a fresh clone with nothing
# configured - no Firebase project, no credentials, no network.
#
# The one value below is only needed for the parts that still talk to Firebase:
# the upload zone, and the older subject/detail pages.

# Base URL of the deployed Cloud Functions, WITH a trailing slash.
#
# Leave it empty and those pages say so plainly. Previously an unset value was
# concatenated into the URL, producing a request to "undefinedgetGeoJson?..." and
# a 404 that looked like a broken server rather than missing configuration.
#
# The functions declare no region, so they deploy to Firebase's default:
#   deployed:  https://us-central1-gzvka-12a9f.cloudfunctions.net/
#   emulator:  http://localhost:5001/gzvka-12a9f/us-central1/
#
# One trap worth knowing: functions/src/utils/cors-helper.ts allows exactly
# "http://localhost:5173" and "https://gzvka.com". Open the site at localhost,
# never at 127.0.0.1, or the browser blocks every backend response even though
# the URL is correct.
VITE_BASE_URL_GF=
